Most likely you did not correctly fetched CSV values and thus your data are incorrect. fgetcsv/fputcsv are notably buggy. You should use instead CsvRfc library - https://github.com/ajgarlag/AjglCsvRfc . What you are trying to do with regards to insert is bad idea. This will incur a huge load on your database since insert_records essentially does call to insert_record in the loop. If amount of records is minimal and it is one time thing OK. But if you plan on running this more often with large record-sets I would reconsider. What I propose should be better for your DB health and faster (Applies ONLY to MySQL and my sql i extension): 
```text
// Prepare massive insert SQL in the format:


// INSERT INTO {table} ('col1', 'col2', 'col3') VALUES(v1, v2, v3);


// INSERT INTO {table} ('col1', 'col2', 'col3') VALUES(v1, v2, v3);


// etc.
```
 Also you would have to ensure your query is not too big since rdbms has a limit on how long a command it can take at a time. You might need to split records in batches like every 300 items before execution etc.

