example of shimming jquery blockUI
assuming you have: 
```text
yourtheme/
javascript
/jquery.blockUI.js
```
 in your theme config.php: 
```text
$THEME->javascripts_footer = array(
    'customjsfile'
);
```
 in yourtheme/javascript/customjsfile.js : 
```text
requirejs.config({
    paths: {
        "jquery.blockUI": '/theme/ouaclean/javascript/jquery.blockUI',
    },
    shim: {
        'jquery.blockui' : {deps: ['jquery']}
    }
});
```
 in your amd module you now should be able to: <pre> require(["jquery.blockUI"], </pre> It's a bit fiddly, and i think there is a theoretical timing issue with how the javascripts load (the customjs has to load before requirejs)
the wrapping method describes above is simpler and cleaner, for the issue with futureproofing i've found diifing the file works fine, and copying the contents is similar to copying the new version of the file, so it hasnt been as messy as i was expecting.

