Well, I know it's a late answer for the original question, but for the next person that comes looking: You have two options that I can see: 1) create a subclass that extends the class you want custom validation for, and override the validate method: 
```text
class admin_setting_configtext_custom extends 
admin_setting_configtext {


    public function validate($data) {


        // your custom validation logic here


    }


}
```
 This probably makes sense to do if you only need custom behaviour for one or two of several settings or setting types. 2) If you need custom validation for most of your fields, look into using an external admin settings page .

