_customdata allows you to pass extra data into a form. When you create an instance of the form, you can specify some arbitrary custom data like this: `$form = new my_form_class(null, $mycustomdata);` Then, anywhere inside the form, you can write: `$mycustomdata = $this->_customdata;` Usually, the data is passed in as an array (it doesn't have to be, it is just the most common way of using it), e.g. 
```text
$mycustomdata = [


  'item1' => $somevar,


  'item2' => $someothervar,


];


$form = new my_form_class(null, $mycustomdata);
```
 Then, inside the form: `$somevar = $this->_customdata['item1'];`

