This is really not that big deal. A decent example of writing custom event(s) can be found in blocks/comments/classes As for listeners you can find one example in blocks/recent_activity/classes. Bottom line for the listeners: Create directory classes inside your custom plugin and in it add file observer.php. In that file declare class named <my plugin component name>_observer and add listeners to whatever events you may need, List of existing events can be found here https://docs.moodle.org/dev/Event_2#Existing_events Create file events.php in db directory of your custom plugin (in there you define bindings of your event listeners to the actual events) The case you explained would most likely involve use of core\event\course_completed event. Let us assume that you have plugin located in blocks/foo which means it's component name is block_foo so therefore: 
```text
// content of file located in blocks/foo/db/events.php
$observers = array (
    array(
        'eventname' => '\core\event\course_completed',
        'callback'  => 'block_foo_observer::course_completed',
    ),
    // Add more if needed.
);

// Content of file located in blocks/foo/classes/observer.php
class block_foo_observer {
    public static function course_completed(\core\event\course_completed $event) {
        // Do something here.
    }
}
```
 And that's it.

