Anything is possible Helson although you should avoid updating configuration values directly in database. In any case if you need to enforce reading of some configuration value from database this is the process: 
```text
function get_dbconfig($name, $plugin=null) {
    global $CFG;

    if (empty($plugin)) {
        $plugin = "core";
        unset($CFG->$name);
    }

    cache_helper::invalidate_by_definition('core', 'config', array(), $plugin);

    return get_config($name, $plugin);
}
```
 Have in mind that this invalidates caching and would make things slower.

