Some time ago I posted a helper function that enabled users to add easily fullname of a user into SQL query based on current moodle settings. Here is the updated version that works on Moodle 2.0-2.7+: 
```text
function sql_fullname($nameas = null) {
    global $DB, $CFG;
    if (is_callable('get_all_user_name_fields')) {
        $data = (object)get_all_user_name_fields();
    } else {
        $data = (object)array('firstname' => 'firstname', 'lastname' => 'lastname');
    }
    $fullname = fullname($data);
    $fields = explode(' ', $fullname);
    $fullname = '';
    $previous = '';
    foreach ($fields as $field) {
        if (($fullname == '') && ($previous == '')) {
            $previous = $field;
        } else {
            if ($previous !== '') {
                $fullname = $previous;
                $previous = '';
            }
            $fullname = $DB->sql_fullname($fullname, $field);
        }
    }

    if (!empty($nameas)) {
        $fullname .= " AS {$nameas}";
    }

    return $fullname;
}

// Usage.
$res = $DB->get_records('user', array('id' => $userid), '', 'id, username, '.sql_fullname('fullname'));
// This generates query like this:
SELECT id, username, CONCAT(firstname, ' ', lastname) AS fullname FROM mdl_user WHERE id = ?
```

